Generated Web Components light theme based on bootstrap design system

Platform: Ignite UI for Blazor

**Color Luminance Warnings:**

The following colors have extreme luminance values that may produce suboptimal shade generation:

| Color | Value | Luminance | Issue |
|-------|-------|-----------|-------|
| primary | `#1a2744` | 0.02 | Too dark - lighter shades (50-200) will lack contrast range |
| surface | `#f0f2f5` | 0.89 | Too light - darker shades (600-900) will appear washed out |

**Recommendation:** For production-quality results, use the `create_custom_palette` tool from the Ignite UI Theming MCP with explicit shade values for these colors. This gives you fine-grained control over each shade level (50-900, A100-A700).

The generated code below uses the standard `palette()` function, which may produce limited shade ranges for the flagged colors.

Variables created/used: $palette, $type-scale, $material-elevations

```scss
// Generated by Ignite UI Theming MCP Server
// Platform: Ignite UI for Web Components

// Import the theming module
// NOTE: @use rules must be at the top of the file. Deduplicate when combining multiple outputs.
/*
 * ⚠️ PALETTE SUITABILITY WARNINGS
 * The following colors have extreme luminance that may produce suboptimal shade generation:
 *   - primary (#1a2744): luminance 0.02 - too dark - lighter shades may lack range
 *   - surface (#f0f2f5): luminance 0.89 - too light - darker shades may be washed out
 * Consider using the create_custom_palette tool of the Ignite UI Theming MCP server with explicit shade values for better results.
 */

@use 'igniteui-theming' as *;
@use 'igniteui-theming/sass/typography/presets/bootstrap' as *;
@use 'igniteui-theming/sass/elevations/presets' as *;

// Custom color palette
$primary-color: #1a2744;
$secondary-color: #00b4d8;
$surface-color: #f0f2f5;

$my-palette: palette(
  $primary: $primary-color,
  $secondary: $secondary-color,
  $surface: $surface-color
);

// Theme configuration
@mixin theme($palette, $variant) {
  // Root-level CSS custom properties
  @property --_progress-integer {
    syntax: '<integer>';
    initial-value: 0;
    inherits: true;
  }

  @property --_progress-fraction {
    syntax: '<integer>';
    initial-value: 0;
    inherits: true;
  }

  :root {
    --ig-theme: #{map.get($palette, '_meta', 'variant')};
    --ig-theme-variant: #{$variant};
    --ig-size-small: 1;
    --ig-size-medium: 2;
    --ig-size-large: 3;
    --ig-scrollbar-size: #{rem(16px)};
  }

  body[dir='rtl'] {
    --ig-dir: -1;
  }

  @include palette($palette);
  @include elevations($material-elevations);
  @include typography(
    $font-family: "'"Inter", "Segoe UI", sans-serif'",
    $type-scale: $type-scale
  );
  @include spacing();
}

// Apply the theme
@include theme($my-palette, 'light');
```

> **File placement:** `@use` rules must appear at the very top of the `.scss` file, before any other statements. When combining outputs from multiple tools, keep only one `@use` per module path.

